course: dictionary
lesson: 884
title: Biology: the study of living things
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Biology is a school subject. It is the study of living things, like plants, animals and people, and how they live and grow. The word has two parts: «bio» means life, and «-logy» means the study of something. So biology is the study of life.
explain: Biology asks how and why. «Rhinos eat only plants (grass, leaves, shoots), never cake.» A biology lesson explains what a rhino eats, and why its body needs those plants to live and grow.
explain: Context helps you here too. In «marine biology», the word marine tells you the biology is about the sea. Read the words near biology, and they show you which living things the sentence is about.
fact: Biology is the study of living things and how they live and grow.
fact: «Bio» means life, and «-logy» means the study of something.
fact: The biology of a living thing is how its body works.
fact: Rhino horns are made of keratin, the same stuff as hair and fingernails.
fact: Baleen is rows of bristly plates in a whale's mouth that sieve out tiny krill and small fish from the water.
exercise: What is biology? | The study of numbers and sums | The study of stars and planets | *The study of living things, like plants, animals and people | The study of rocks and the earth
exercise: What does the «bio» in biology mean? | *Life | Rock | Light | Money
exercise: «Camels can go many days without drinking because their bodies waste very little water.» Is this a biology question? | *Yes, it asks how a living body works | No, it is about maps | Yes, but only if it is about cakes | No, it is about sums
test: In «marine biology», what does marine mean? | Lost | Very small | *To do with the sea | To do with the sky
test: Baleen is best described as? | *Rows of bristly plates that sieve tiny krill and fish | A set of sharp teeth for biting seals | A kind of soft fur | A small tail fin
exam: Which of these best describes biology? | A school subject about reading poems | A school subject about maps and countries | A school subject about money and shops | *A school subject that studies living things and how their bodies work
